TALLY_FINAL_MESSAGE={"verdict":"retry","diagnosis":"Failed the ownership check conflict-domains because the task run left untracked artifacts under the repo-root path .build/, which is outside the authorized prefixes container and results/receipts: container/build.sh defaults CCACHE_DIR_HOST to \"$REPO_ROOT/.build/ccache\" and PIP_CACHE_HOST to \"$REPO_ROOT/.build/pip-cache\", then mkdir -p creates them inside the worktree, and the attempt also dropped .build/build.log there; git status shows the whole .build/ tree as untracked, so the driver reported \"agent left uncommitted changes\" and the ownership gate rejected the attempt. The committed source files themselves (container/Containerfile, container/build.sh, container/rootfs/.keep, results/receipts/build.json at d89f338) are all inside the boundary, so the defect is confined to where the script materializes caches and logs plus the leftover working-tree state. Fix on attempt 2, touching only container/build.sh: (1) default the host cache paths outside the repository — e.g. CCACHE_DIR_HOST=\"${FN_CCACHE_DIR:-${XDG_CACHE_HOME:-$HOME/.cache}/flashnext/ccache}\" and PIP_CACHE_HOST=\"${FN_PIP_CACHE_DIR:-${XDG_CACHE_HOME:-$HOME/.cache}/flashnext/pip}\" — keeping the FN_CCACHE_DIR / FN_PIP_CACHE_DIR overrides and the same podman --volume wiring so the overnight-iteration and one-line-patch-rebuild behavior is unchanged; (2) update the header comment block that advertises the \".build/ccache next to this repo\" default to match the new location; (3) do not write any log file into the repo — if a build log is wanted, send it to the same out-of-tree cache dir or leave it to the caller's redirection. Before finishing, delete the stray .build/ tree from the worktree (rm -rf .build) so nothing outside container/ and results/receipts/ is created, modified, or left uncommitted, then commit only container/ and results/receipts/ paths. The acceptance criterion recipe-pins is unaffected by this change: bash -n still passes and the grep-checked strings (torch==2.13.0+rocm7.14.0, repo.amd.com/rocm/whl-multi-arch, mecattaf/vllm, flashnext:dev, MIT) all remain in place."}
